# Settings for the language packs' nightly translation on the build host
# (scripts/langpacks-nightly.mjs). scripts/chain/install-langpacks.sh writes
# /etc/filex-langpacks.env from this file, with LANGPACKS_ROOT filled in, and
# never over one; FILEX_LANGPACKS_ENV or --env name another. KEY=VALUE, no
# expansion; the process environment wins over this file.
#
# ⚠ No secret is a value here: a key or a token is the FILE it is in, read
# when it is used and never logged. Hosts and URLs below are placeholders.

# ── where it lives ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything of the run, outside every repository: the pack checkouts
# (filex-lang-*, cloned by the installer), the tree (made and removed per
# run), the nights (worklists, the agent's directories and logs), last.json,
# history.jsonl and the agent's own HOME.
LANGPACKS_ROOT=/var/lib/filex-langpacks
# The nightly test run's checkout: its objects, and its fetch credential, are
# what the tree is made from. The tree lives outside it (the nightly run
# cleans its checkout with git clean every night).
# LANGPACKS_FILEX=/var/lib/filex-nightly/src
# LANGPACKS_WORKTREE=/var/lib/filex-langpacks/tree
# LANGPACKS_KEEP_TREE=0
# The pack checkouts, colon-separated. Empty: the filex-lang-* checkouts
# beside the tree, the template excepted.
# LANGPACKS_PACKS=
# LANGPACKS_KEEP_NIGHTS=14
# The time zone a night is named in (default: this host's).
LANGPACKS_TZ=Europe/Istanbul

# ── what is translated ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The commit translated against: a ref of that checkout - origin/main, the
# default, fetched alone first (LANGPACKS_FETCH=0 does not fetch); `night`,
# the commit the nightly run ran on (LANGPACKS_FALLBACK_REF when it named none
# the checkout has); or `none`, the checkout's working tree as it stands.
# LANGPACKS_REF=origin/main
# LANGPACKS_FETCH=1
# LANGPACKS_FALLBACK_REF=origin/main
# Another catalogue to translate against: a directory holding
# filex-catalogue-en.json and filex-catalogue-context.json, or vX.Y.Z (a
# release's). Empty: the tree's own.
# LANGPACKS_CATALOGUE=

# ── when ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The nightly run's tonight.json: the run waits while it says the night is
# going and its process is alive, at most LANGPACKS_WAIT_MAX_MIN, looking every
# LANGPACKS_WAIT_POLL_MIN. A night that did not start is not waited for.
# Empty: no wait.
# LANGPACKS_NIGHT_FILE=/var/lib/filex-nightly/nightly/tonight.json
# LANGPACKS_WAIT_MAX_MIN=150
# LANGPACKS_WAIT_POLL_MIN=5
# LANGPACKS_NIGHT_MAX_AGE_H=20
# The whole run's minutes, the wait included: a pack not started by then is
# left for the next night. filex-langpacks.service allows a little more.
# LANGPACKS_BUDGET_MIN=330

# ── the agent ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Claude Code, started in the pack's directory of copies with the boundary of
# scripts/lib/langpacks-nightly.mjs claudeArgs (no command or web tool, no MCP
# server, file tools confined to that directory) and a HOME of its own. The
# model is always named: a session without one takes the CLI's default, which
# an account may have no plan for.
# LANGPACKS_AGENT_BIN=claude
# LANGPACKS_AGENT_MODEL=opus
# More arguments for it, separated by spaces (--effort high, for example).
# LANGPACKS_AGENT_ARGS=
# Minutes per session, and how many times refused answers go back to it.
# LANGPACKS_AGENT_TIMEOUT_MIN=45
# LANGPACKS_FIX_ROUNDS=1
# LANGPACKS_AGENT_HOME=/var/lib/filex-langpacks/agent-home
# Its credential: the project's Claude account, asked from the work server's
# MCP `account.credential` at every run with a project token read from the
# file - no copy of the credential is kept on the host.
LANGPACKS_WORK_URL=https://work.example.com/mcp/work
LANGPACKS_WORK_TOKEN_FILE=/root/.config/filex-langpacks/work-mcp.token
# Needed only with a token that is not confined to the project.
# LANGPACKS_WORK_PROJECT=<project id>
# Or, for a run by hand, a file holding a Claude Code token (claude
# setup-token), given to the agent alone as CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN.
# LANGPACKS_CLAUDE_TOKEN_FILE=/root/.config/filex-langpacks/claude.token
# Another agent altogether: a command line the shell runs in the directory of
# copies, with the prompt on its stdin and the worklist's path in
# LANGPACKS_WORKLIST. It replaces Claude Code and its boundary: give it one.
# LANGPACKS_AGENT_CMD=
# The trailer of the packs' commits (empty: none).
# LANGPACKS_TRAILER=Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

# ── who is told (scripts/lib/notify.mjs) ────────────────────────────────────
# changes (the default): unless nothing was pending; always; off.
# LANGPACKS_NOTIFY=changes
# A person: a JSON POST {group, source, severity, title, message} with a
# Bearer key read from the file - the test chain's own key will do.
# FILEX_NOTIFY_URL=https://notify.example.com/api/notify/v1/send
# FILEX_NOTIFY_KEY_FILE=/var/lib/filex-chain/notify.key
# FILEX_NOTIFY_GROUP=infra
# FILEX_NOTIFY_SOURCE=filex-langpacks
# An agent: an MCP server's `notify` tool, once per name in FILEX_WAKE_AGENT.
# FILEX_WAKE_URL=https://work.example.com/mcp/work
# FILEX_WAKE_TOKEN_FILE=/root/.config/filex-langpacks/work-mcp.token
# FILEX_WAKE_AGENT=release-session
# FILEX_WAKE_PROJECT=<project id>
